What is adapted from it here (issue #729): the dashboard part of the pages
skill (internal/controlplane/clientcli/skills/pages/): the build steps, the
critique order and the rules of its SKILL.md in pages's SKILL.md, and its
references perception.md, layout.md, tokens.md, components.md, snippets.md and
qa.md as the files of the same names in references/, each naming what changed
in its header. Changed: written for one plain HTML page in the artifact's
locked frame, so the React and Tailwind snippets are plain JavaScript and CSS
on the same tokens, charts are inline SVG or CSS and nothing is loaded from the
network; the page cannot act, so an action is offered in the chat reply; one
notes section is allowed at the end of a report (owner, 2026-11-17); the
screenshot pass uses the widths an artifact is seen at. The template
(dashboard.html) follows its rules: tokens for light and dark, a KPI row with
deltas, loading, empty and error states, one tooltip, and a check that the
tiles, charts and tables agree, after the totals its examples expose to a test.
Left out: swiftui.md (Bots make web pages), the range calendar, the Tailwind
notes, the case studies, sources.md (its sources are named in perception.md),
the README, the example pages and images, the plugin files, and the sign-off
line.
